        "prompt": "$3xyz-12xy^2z$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$3xyz(1-4y)$",
          "worked": "$\\begin{aligned}3xyz-12xy^2z&=3xyz\\times1-3xyz\\times4y\\\\3xyz-12xy^2z&=3xyz(1-4y)\\end{aligned}$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 18
      },
      {
        "id": "p9-q6-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "$16a^2bc+4ab^3c$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$4abc(4a+b^2)$",
          "worked": "$\\begin{aligned}16a^2bc+4ab^3c&=4abc\\times4a+4abc\\times b^2\\\\16a^2bc+4ab^3c&=4abc(4a+b^2)\\end{aligned}$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 18
      },
      {
        "id": "p9-q6-c",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "c",
        "prompt": "$8m^2np+20m^2n^3p^4$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$4m^2np(2+5n^2p^3)$\n\nTake out the HCF $4m^2np$.",
          "worked": "The HCF is $4m^2np$.\n\n$\\begin{aligned}8m^2np+20m^2n^3p^4&=4m^2np(2+5n^2p^3)\\end{aligned}$\n\nThe remaining factors are $8m^2np\\div4m^2np=2$ and $20m^2n^3p^4\\div4m^2np=5n^2p^3$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 25
      },
      {
        "id": "p9-q6-d",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "d",
        "prompt": "$9p^2q-3pq+12pq^2$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$3pq(3p-1+4q)$\n\nTake out the HCF $3pq$.",
          "worked": "The HCF is $3pq$.\n\n$\\begin{aligned}9p^2q-3pq+12pq^2&=3pq(3p-1+4q)\\end{aligned}$\n\nDividing the three terms by $3pq$ gives $3p$, $-1$ and $4q$, respectively.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 25
      },
      {
        "id": "p9-q6-e",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "e",
        "prompt": "$5a^2b+20abc+15ab^2c$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$5ab(a+4c+3bc)$\n\nTake out the HCF $5ab$.",
          "worked": "The HCF is $5ab$.\n\n$\\begin{aligned}5a^2b+20abc+15ab^2c&=5ab(a+4c+3bc)\\end{aligned}$\n\nDividing the three terms by $5ab$ gives $a$, $4c$ and $3bc$, respectively.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 25
      }
